PART 3 -- THE COMBINED STATEMENT: ONE r^-1 LAW, AMPLITUDE M500^-0.41, ACROSS 1e13-9e14
====================================================================================================
  THE RISE vs MASS (12 cluster + 26 group slopes, n = 38):
    d s/d log10(M500/8e14) = -0.137 +- 0.053  (Spearman rho = -0.418, p = 0.009)
    -> the rise is FLAT-TO-STEEPER toward low mass: s(8e14) ~ +0.23, s(1e13) ~ +0.49

  THE AMPLITUDE RUN IS MEASURED (not fitted per-cluster):
    q = -0.414 +- 0.157 on the 12 committed per-cluster amplitudes (Spearman rho = -0.587, p = 0.045);
    pooled 96-bin 3-param refit: q = -0.414 +- 0.090, p = +0.990 +- 0.035, c0 = -0.145 +- 0.036
    GROUP anchors (this lane): (i) a_c predicted 1.4-5.8 at M500 = 5e12-1.7e14 (median 2.47) -- the run extended 1.5 dex down in mass;
    (ii) the rise measured +0.536 (median +0.609) vs cluster +0.235: same-or-steeper CONFIRMED (20/26 above);
    (iii) the level face: f_gas(R500) drops +0.341 +- 0.210 dex/dex toward 1e13 (median 0.06 at groups vs 0.15 at clusters).

  THE TWO-PARAMETER DUST LAW (the thorn's freedom, final state):
    c_dust(M500, r/R500) = 10^(-0.144 +- 0.030) x (M500/8e14)^(-0.414 +- 0.157) x (r/R500)^(-1.0)
    = 0.72 x (M500/8e14)^-0.41 x (r/R500)^-1  -- TWO parameters, both MEASURED;
    residual floor: 0.097 dex (one shape + per-cluster amp) / 0.119 dex (3-param literal form, 96 bins) -- G122's committed 0.097 / 0.119
    group-scale verification to 1e13: the rise slope +0.536 (this lane) closes the envelope statement

